IMPORT prelude

-- Gambling Control Act 2022 (Singapore) -- what social gambling is (s 12), who is an underaged individual (s 13), the offences
-- an ordinary punter, young person, excluded person or unlicensed operator meets (ss 18-37, selected), their defences and
-- their maximum penalties.
--
-- Edition: Gambling Control Act 2022 (No. 15 of 2022), informal consolidation "current version as at 01 Oct 2026", as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/GCA2022.txt, with amendments to Act 29 of 2024 (in force 21 September 2026)
-- shown. The Act is not part of the 2020 Revised Edition.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 9 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the offences in Part 2 and the
-- two definitions they turn on. Not encoded: who is exempt or licensed under s 18(1) beyond a flag, the meaning of
-- "gambling", "betting", "game of chance" and "lottery" (ss 4-11), possession (s 15), advertising (ss 85-87), interference
-- offences (ss 38, 39), forfeiture (ss 40, 41), presumptions (Part 3), licensing and approvals (Parts 4, 5), entry bans and
-- sanctions (Parts 6, 7), and anything left to Regulations (prescribed conditions, raised ages, countable offences).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the other naive rows (the writing-l4-rules
-- skill was not loadable in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Gambling Control Act 2022 -- offences`

§§ `12 -- social gambling`

-- s 12(1): NON-REMOTE gambling which "(a) is conducted by an individual in premises that are either the individual's home or
-- another individual's home in Singapore; (b) has as participants only individuals who are members of the same family or who
-- know each other personally; (c) is substantially spontaneous, even though it may occur regularly, habitually or by
-- arrangement ...; (d) is not promoted or conducted (i) by or for the private gain of any person not participating in the
-- gambling; or (ii) in the course of any business; (e) is conducted so that the only way a participant ... can make a profit
-- or gain any other benefit as a result of the gambling is by winning; and (f) is conducted in accordance with the conditions
-- prescribed (if any) by Regulations, is to be taken to constitute social gambling and is not unlawful."
DECLARE Game HAS
    `is remote gambling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is at an individual's home in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has only family or personal acquaintances playing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is substantially spontaneous` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is promoted for the gain of a non-participant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is conducted in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lets players profit only by winning` IS A BOOLEAN
    `breaches a condition prescribed by Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the game` IS A Game
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the game is social gambling` IF
        (NOT `the game`'s `is remote gambling`)
    AND `the game`'s `is at an individual's home in Singapore`
    AND `the game`'s `has only family or personal acquaintances playing`
    AND `the game`'s `is substantially spontaneous`
    AND (NOT `the game`'s `is promoted for the gain of a non-participant`)
    AND (NOT `the game`'s `is conducted in the course of a business`)
    AND `the game`'s `lets players profit only by winning`
    AND (NOT `the game`'s `breaches a condition prescribed by Regulations`)

§§ `13 -- underaged individuals`

-- s 13(1) table: on-course betting 18; off-course betting 18; place-based gambling involving a lottery, or sports betting
-- (not a horse or pony race at a racecourse) where "a live broadcast of the sporting event is not provided at the premises",
-- 18; place-based sports betting WITH a live broadcast at the premises, 21; "Any other type of non-remote gambling or remote
-- gambling that is (a) not mentioned in item 1, 2, 3 or 4 (even if carried on within a casino); (b) not authorised by a class
-- licence; and (c) not social gambling", 21. Each age may be raised by order (s 13(2)); no order was retrieved.
--
-- Class-licensed gambling and social gambling fall in no item of the table, so on this reading no one taking part in them is
-- an underaged individual. That is an inference from the table's structure; the Act does not say so in terms.
DECLARE GamblingKind IS ONE OF
    `on-course betting`
    `off-course betting`
    `buying a lottery ticket at a retail outlet`
    `sports betting at an outlet with no live broadcast`
    `sports betting at a venue showing a live broadcast`
    `playing a gaming machine in a gaming machine room`
    `playing an online game of chance`
    `playing at a casino`
    `a game authorised by a class licence`
    `a social game at home`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A GamblingKind
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the minimum age under s 13` IS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `on-course betting` THEN 18
    WHEN `off-course betting` THEN 18
    WHEN `buying a lottery ticket at a retail outlet` THEN 18
    WHEN `sports betting at an outlet with no live broadcast` THEN 18
    WHEN `sports betting at a venue showing a live broadcast` THEN 21
    WHEN `playing a gaming machine in a gaming machine room` THEN 21
    WHEN `playing an online game of chance` THEN 21
    WHEN `playing at a casino` THEN 21
    WHEN `a game authorised by a class licence` THEN 0
    WHEN `a social game at home` THEN 0

GIVEN `the kind` IS A GamblingKind, `age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gambler is an underaged individual` IF
    `age in years` < `the minimum age under s 13` `the kind`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A GamblingKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is social gambling kind` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a social game at home` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the kind` IS A GamblingKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is casino kind` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `playing at a casino` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `30 to 35 -- underaged individuals and young persons`

-- s 31(1): "An underaged individual must not engage in gambling in or from Singapore." (2): fine not exceeding $1,500. (5): the
-- underaged individual "must not be imprisoned, or detained in a detention centre, as a consequence of a failure to pay a fine".
-- (7): "This section does not apply to gambling within any casino or to social gambling."
GIVEN `the kind` IS A GamblingKind, `age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the underaged gambler commits an offence under s 31` IF
        `the gambler is an underaged individual` `the kind` `age in years`
    AND (NOT `is casino kind` `the kind`)
    AND (NOT `is social gambling kind` `the kind`)

-- s 30(1): a person commits an offence if the person "(a) engages in gambling (that is not social gambling) with an underaged
-- individual". (2): not guilty if the accused proves "(a) had reasonable grounds to believe and did make reasonable inquiries
-- to ascertain that [the gambler] was not an underaged individual; or (b) had received from the gambler evidence purporting to
-- show that the gambler was not an underaged individual, and that it was reasonable to and the accused did accept that evidence
-- as correct." (3): $300,000 or 6 years or both. (5) strict liability. s 30 has no casino carve-out of the kind in s 31(7).
GIVEN `the kind` IS A GamblingKind, `age in years` IS A NUMBER,
      `made reasonable inquiries on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonably accepted evidence of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `gambling with the individual is an offence under s 30` IF
        `the gambler is an underaged individual` `the kind` `age in years`
    AND (NOT `is social gambling kind` `the kind`)
    AND (NOT `made reasonable inquiries on reasonable grounds`)
    AND (NOT `reasonably accepted evidence of age`)

-- s 32(1)(a): an underaged individual must not "intentionally enter or remain in any approved gambling venue during a restricted
-- period". (5): not guilty if they prove they "did not know or could not reasonably have known" it was such a venue, or were
-- complying with a direction of a police officer or other public officer. (7): for this section and s 33, "approved gambling
-- venue" EXCLUDES premises where place-based gambling is lawfully provided involving "(a) participating in any lottery; or (b)
-- betting connected with a sporting event ... at which a live broadcast of the sporting event is not provided".
DECLARE VenueKind IS ONE OF
    `a lottery retail outlet`
    `a sports betting outlet with no live broadcast`
    `a sports betting venue showing a live broadcast`

GIVEN `the venue` IS A VenueKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts as an approved gambling venue for s 32` IF
    CONSIDER `the venue`
    WHEN `a sports betting venue showing a live broadcast` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the venue` IS A VenueKind, `is underaged` IS A BOOLEAN, `entered intentionally during a restricted period` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `could not reasonably have known it was a venue` IS A BOOLEAN, `was obeying an official direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the underaged entry is an offence under s 32` IF
        `is underaged`
    AND `counts as an approved gambling venue for s 32` `the venue`
    AND `entered intentionally during a restricted period`
    AND (NOT `could not reasonably have known it was a venue`)
    AND (NOT `was obeying an official direction`)

-- s 35(1): a person who employs "an individual who is below 21 years of age (called in this section a young person) to conduct a
-- betting operation, gaming or a lottery" commits an offence; $300,000 or 6 years or both. (3) defences of reasonable inquiry
-- or reasonably accepted evidence, as in s 30. (4): nothing prohibits a licensee or class licensee employing a young person "to
-- perform any managerial, clerical, secretarial or administrative work that is wholly performed within enclosed premises".
GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER, `employer is a licensee or class licensee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the work is office work wholly within enclosed premises` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `employed to conduct gambling` IS A BOOLEAN, `made reasonable inquiries or accepted evidence of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employment is an offence under s 35` IF
        `age in years` < 21
    AND `employed to conduct gambling`
    AND (NOT (`employer is a licensee or class licensee` AND `the work is office work wholly within enclosed premises`))
    AND (NOT `made reasonable inquiries or accepted evidence of age`)

§§ `20 and 26 -- punters and people found in gambling places`

-- s 20(1): an individual commits an offence if he gambles with B using B's gambling service, B is providing it in
-- contravention of s 18(1), and the individual "knows, or ought reasonably to have known" that. (2): likewise gambling in a
-- place he "knows, or ought reasonably to have known" is an unlawful gambling place. (3): $10,000 or 6 months or both.
GIVEN `provider is unlicensed under s 18` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or ought to have known it was unlicensed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `gambled in an unlawful gambling place` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or ought to have known of the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the punter commits an offence under s 20` IF
        (`provider is unlicensed under s 18` AND `knew or ought to have known it was unlicensed`)
    OR  (`gambled in an unlawful gambling place` AND `knew or ought to have known of the place`)

-- s 26(1): "An individual who is found in, or who enters or leaves, an unlawful gambling place commits an offence." (2): not
-- guilty if he proves "(a) he or she did not know and had no reasonable cause to suspect ... and as soon as practicable after
-- becoming aware ... took all reasonable steps to leave"; or "(b) ... was in ... the unlawful gambling place for a lawful
-- purpose or with other reasonable excuse." (3): $10,000 or 6 months or both. (5) strict liability.
GIVEN `found in the place` IS A BOOLEAN, `did not know and left promptly on learning` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `was there for a lawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `being there is an offence under s 26` IF
        `found in the place`
    AND (NOT `did not know and left promptly on learning`)
    AND (NOT `was there for a lawful purpose`)

§§ `18 to 37 -- maximum penalties`

-- Operator-tier offences (ss 18, 19, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 27(1)-(3), 36): "liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- $500,000 and shall also be punished with imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years; but (b) where the person is a repeat
-- offender ... $700,000 and shall also be punished with imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years."
-- Where the contravention is "by engaging in conduct described in section 6(2), 8(3) or 10(2)" (conduct "on behalf of, or in
-- accordance with arrangements made by, another") ss 18, 19, 22, 24, 25 and (8(3) only) 27 drop to $200,000 and 5 years, or
-- $300,000 and 7 years for a repeat offender. ss 21, 23 and 36 have no such lower tier.
-- s 37 (credit for unlawful gambling): $200,000 and 4 years; repeat $300,000 and 7 years.
-- Every one of these uses "and shall also be punished with imprisonment": a custodial term is mandatory.
-- Punter-tier offences: "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both" (ss 20, 26,
-- 27(5)); 12 months for s 28 proxy gambling and for excluded persons (ss 31(4), 32(4)); 3 years for an excluded person's false
-- evidence (s 33(3)). ss 30, 34, 35: $300,000 or 6 years or both. Underaged individuals: $1,500 (ss 31(2), 32(3)) and $10,000
-- for false evidence of age (s 33(1)), with no imprisonment and none in default of payment (ss 31(5), 32(8), 33(2)).
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 18 conducting gambling without a licence`
    `s 19 conducting gambling outside an approved venue`
    `s 21 financial interest in an unlawful gambling service`
    `s 22 conducting an unapproved game`
    `s 23 owner or occupier of an unlawful gambling place`
    `s 24 organising an unlawful gambling place`
    `s 25 financing an unlawful gambling place`
    `s 27 operating a prohibited or unapproved gaming machine`
    `s 36 possessing unlawful gambling instruments`
    `s 37 providing credit for unlawful gambling`
    `s 20 gambling with an unlicensed provider`
    `s 26 being in an unlawful gambling place`
    `s 27(5) playing a prohibited gaming machine`
    `s 28 proxy gambling outside a gaming machine room`
    `s 30 gambling with an underaged individual`
    `s 34 inducing an underaged individual to gamble`
    `s 35 employing a young person in gambling`
    `s 31(2) gambling while underaged`
    `s 31(4) gambling while excluded`
    `s 32(3) underaged entry to a venue`
    `s 32(4) excluded person in a gaming machine room`
    `s 33(1) underaged false evidence of age`
    `s 33(3) excluded person false evidence`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a top-tier operator offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 18 conducting gambling without a licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 19 conducting gambling outside an approved venue` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 21 financial interest in an unlawful gambling service` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 22 conducting an unapproved game` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 23 owner or occupier of an unlawful gambling place` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 24 organising an unlawful gambling place` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 25 financing an unlawful gambling place` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 27 operating a prohibited or unapproved gaming machine` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 36 possessing unlawful gambling instruments` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a lower tier for conduct on behalf of another` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 18 conducting gambling without a licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 19 conducting gambling outside an approved venue` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 22 conducting an unapproved game` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 24 organising an unlawful gambling place` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 25 financing an unlawful gambling place` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 27 operating a prohibited or unapproved gaming machine` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment is mandatory` IF
        `is a top-tier operator offence` `the offence`
    OR  CONSIDER `the offence`
        WHEN `s 37 providing credit for unlawful gambling` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `first` IS A NUMBER, `repeat` IS A NUMBER, `is repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `by record` IS
    IF `is repeat` THEN `repeat` ELSE `first`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `on behalf of another` IS A BOOLEAN, `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `takes the lower tier` IF
    `has a lower tier for conduct on behalf of another` `the offence` AND `on behalf of another`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `on behalf of another` IS A BOOLEAN, `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine` IS
    IF `takes the lower tier` `the offence` `on behalf of another` `repeat offender`
        THEN `by record` 200000 300000 `repeat offender`
        ELSE `the maximum fine above the lower tier` `the offence` `repeat offender`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine above the lower tier` IS
    IF `is a top-tier operator offence` `the offence`
        THEN `by record` 500000 700000 `repeat offender`
        ELSE `the maximum fine for other offences` `the offence` `repeat offender`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine for other offences` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 37 providing credit for unlawful gambling` THEN `by record` 200000 300000 `repeat offender`
    WHEN `s 30 gambling with an underaged individual` THEN 300000
    WHEN `s 34 inducing an underaged individual to gamble` THEN 300000
    WHEN `s 35 employing a young person in gambling` THEN 300000
    WHEN `s 31(2) gambling while underaged` THEN 1500
    WHEN `s 32(3) underaged entry to a venue` THEN 1500
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `on behalf of another` IS A BOOLEAN, `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS
    IF `takes the lower tier` `the offence` `on behalf of another` `repeat offender`
        THEN `by record` 60 84 `repeat offender`
        ELSE `the maximum imprisonment above the lower tier` `the offence` `repeat offender`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment above the lower tier` IS
    IF `is a top-tier operator offence` `the offence`
        THEN `by record` 84 120 `repeat offender`
        ELSE `the maximum imprisonment for other offences` `the offence` `repeat offender`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment for other offences` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 37 providing credit for unlawful gambling` THEN `by record` 48 84 `repeat offender`
    WHEN `s 30 gambling with an underaged individual` THEN 72
    WHEN `s 34 inducing an underaged individual to gamble` THEN 72
    WHEN `s 35 employing a young person in gambling` THEN 72
    WHEN `s 28 proxy gambling outside a gaming machine room` THEN 12
    WHEN `s 31(4) gambling while excluded` THEN 12
    WHEN `s 32(4) excluded person in a gaming machine room` THEN 12
    WHEN `s 33(3) excluded person false evidence` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 31(2) gambling while underaged` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 32(3) underaged entry to a venue` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 33(1) underaged false evidence of age` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 6
